      "headline": "Put Your Habits on Cruise Control with Pre-Decisions",
      "keyInsight": "Most people think beating procrastination requires immense daily willpower and constant focus. In reality, relying on willpower in the heat of the moment is a losing game. When you are tired, your brain always picks the couch over the treadmill. The secret weapon is taking choice completely off the table before temptation strikes. You link a specific cue to an immediate action using a simple formula: when X happens, I do Y. If you wait until you feel like starting, you will stall forever. By deciding the exact time and place in advance, your brain acts automatically without debate. It feels like setting an automatic thermostat in your house. The temperature drops, the heater clicks on, and nobody has to argue about turning the dial.",
