      "keyInsight": "We treat self-control like an endless power source that should never run dry. Then we wonder why we cave to distractions at eight in the evening. Willpower behaves exactly like a muscle or a fuel tank in your car. Every tough email, awkward phone call, and resisted cookie burns real fuel. By late afternoon, your mental tank runs on empty fumes. If you try to launch your biggest, hardest project when your battery shows two percent, you will fail every time. The trick is not demanding super-human strength from an empty tank. You must spend your best energy on your toughest task first, before the day drains your reserves dry.",
